    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "I take a sealed glass container and remove 80% of the air. Then I remove 80% of the remaining air. I do this process six times altogether. What percentage of the original air is left in the container?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.0064\\%$.",
      "worked": "Each removal leaves $100\\%-80\\%=20\\%$ of the air present before that removal.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Fraction remaining}&=0.2^6\\\\\\text{Percentage remaining}&=0.2^6\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage remaining}&=0.0064\\%\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
